safeguard_memory:incident:connection_pool_exhaustion
The material reports the database connection pool as exhausted, with connections held against a full pool and acquisitions timing out. The mechanism is reported in the material; whether it was caused by connections not being released, by excessive concurrency, or by slow queries is not established by the logs alone and remains a hypothesis.
{"type":"safeguard_memory","memory_id":"safeguard-incident-connection_pool_exhaustion","version":1,"origin_incident_id":"[redacted-uuid]","domain":"incident","action_type":"repeat_failed_operation","failure_category":"connection_pool_exhaustion","verified_failure":"The material reports the database connection pool as exhausted, with connections held against a full pool and acquisitions timing out. The mechanism is reported in the material; whether it was caused by connections not being released, by excessive concurrency, or by slow queries is not established by the logs alone and remains a hypothesis.","evidence":["incident:[redacted-uuid]","incident:submission:[redacted-uuid]"],"corrective_rule":"The material reports the database connection pool as exhausted, with connections held against a full pool and acquisitions timing out. The mechanism is reported in the material; whether it was caused by connections not being released, by excessive concurrency, or by slow queries is not established by the logs alone and remains a hypothesis.","applies_when":["domain=incident","actionType=repeat_failed_operation","failureCategory=connection_pool_exhaustion"],"required_checks":["Exercise a controlled workload with a documented concurrency level and duration, against the same pool configuration.","Measure connection-acquisition latency, pool utilisation, request latency, and the HTTP 5xx rate throughout the run.","Instrument connection acquisition, usage, and release, then replay the incident window to see whether connections are held past their work.","Alert on sustained pool saturation and on rising connection-acquisition latency, so the next occurrence is detected before requests time out.","Run a controlled concurrency test at documented load to determine whether the configured pool capacity is sufficient, and investigate a connection leak if instrumentation shows connections are not released."],"action":"REQUIRE_VERIFICATION","severity":"high","confidence":0.7,"limitations":["Scoped to domain incident and action type repeat_failed_operation; it does not generalise to unrelated operations.","The recommended mechanism assumes the leading hypothesis holds: Database connections may not be released promptly after use, so the pool drains over time. The material does not show acquisition/release pairing, so this is a hypothesis, not a finding.","It is assumed the pool's configured maximum is the intended capacity; the material does not state the configuration or how it was chosen.","It is assumed the reported measurements (active/idle/max) came from the pool under test; their source is not named in the material.","No authoritative source was connected for this submission, so the mechanism is validated against the decision engine's own behaviour rather than against a live system.","The safeguard is scoped to this domain and action type; it does not generalise to unrelated operations."],"authoritative":true,"support_basis":"The material supplies 6 machine-checkable observed fact(s) behind the finding, so the safeguard is grounded in the submitted evidence.","status":"active","provenance":"live"}

corrective_lesson:incident:connection_pool_exhaustion
The material reports the database connection pool as exhausted, with connections held against a full pool and acquisitions timing out. The mechanism is reported in the material; whether it was caused by connections not being released, by excessive concurrency, or by slow queries is not established by the logs alone and remains a hypothesis. Instrument connection acquisition, usage, and release; alert on sustained pool saturation and rising acquisition latency; and treat the pool's capacity as unproven until a controlled concurrency test demonstrates it.
